## How to Use on New Laptop:

### Option 1: Full Copy (includes vendor/ and node_modules/)

# On old laptop
tar -czf z-exam-portable.tar.gz z-exam/

# Copy to new laptop
scp z-exam-portable.tar.gz user@new-laptop:~/

# On new laptop
tar -xzf z-exam-portable.tar.gz
cd z-exam
./start-portable.sh


Option 2: Lightweight Copy (excludes heavy folders)

# On old laptop
tar -czf z-exam-light.tar.gz z-exam/ \
  --exclude=vendor \
  --exclude=node_modules \
  --exclude=public/build \
  --exclude=bootstrap/cache \
  --exclude=postgresql-portable/data \
  --exclude=.git

# On new laptop
tar -xzf z-exam-light.tar.gz
cd z-exam
./setup-portable.sh  # Installs dependencies and builds assets
./start-portable.sh


On Source (Linux/macOS) - Create Lightweight Archive:

# Exclude ALL platform-specific binaries
tar -czf z-exam-light.tar.gz z-exam/ \
  --exclude=vendor \
  --exclude=node_modules \
  --exclude=public/build \
  --exclude=bootstrap/cache \
  --exclude=postgresql-portable/data \
  --exclude=php-portable \
  --exclude=nodejs-portable \
  --exclude=.git

On Target (windows) full rebuild
REM 1. Extract
tar -xzf z-exam-light.tar.gz
cd z-exam

REM 2. Run Windows setup (installs PHP, PostgreSQL, Node.js, RoadRunner)
REM    This also runs: composer install, npm ci, npm run build, migrations
setup-portable.bat

REM 3. Start
start-portable.bat


